             :plan "An eval request of `nil` by a warm agent costs 17.1 MB, 6,617 armed calls and 44 reads; its estimate is 4 MB, 500 calls, 10 reads, 25 ms: read one form, evaluate it, one recording transaction of about ten datoms, print one value. On default the same request measured 33 MB and 6,812 calls with 40 ms in `:settle` (entrance 2.6 MB, step 11.0 MB, writer 7.0 MB, commit 12.7 MB). Find what the step and commit do per request that is not proportional to one form. Read `seon.mcp/eval-clj`, `seon.batch/render-request-cost-ai` and `seon.batch/request-cost`. Measured in a `bin/seon check` JVM at 553c9d5d5 by `seon.cost-estimate-test/ordinary-operations-cost-no-more-than-their-estimates` (row `:unchanged-request` of `seon.cost-estimate-test/estimates`, which also records these numbers as its accepted overrun). Done when the row is within its estimate; then delete the row's `:overrun`. Until then `seon.cost-estimate-test/no-ordinary-operation-grows-past-its-accepted-overrun` (run on every src commit) refuses a commit that grows it past 1.5x."
             :proofs #{seon.cost-estimate-test/ordinary-operations-cost-no-more-than-their-estimates}}
